{
  "quest.045CF1C9896895E7.title": "Farming Tools",
  "quest.5DCA31CA513EF27C.quest_desc": [
    "&eHephaestus&r is all about the Smeltery. You melt metal down, then pour it into whatever shape you need.",
    "",
    "Start with a batch of &aSeared Bricks&r. Every block in this chapter is built from them or from the &2Forge Bricks&r behind them.",
    "",
    "Make more than you think you need. It never hurts to have too many!",
    "",
    "Once your Smeltery is running, the second half of this chapter uses it to cast tools and weapons with &eHephaestus Tools&r.",
  ],
  "quest.6223A2A7C3DCF933.quest_desc": [
    "In this pack, raw ore melts into twice the metal an ingot does: 180 mB instead of 90 mB.",
    "",
    "Melt your &2Raw Ore&r instead of smelting it in a furnace, and each piece casts into two ingots.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Blocks of raw ore melt the same way, nine times over.",
  ],
  "quest.0EEBCA59B2927918.title": "Know Your Metals",
  "quest.34C064CDD789F0B3.quest_desc": [
    "Build a &aSmeltery Controller&r into a wall of &2Seared Bricks&r on a brick floor. Then add a &aSeared Drain&r to the wall to get the metal back out.",
    "",
    "The &aSmeltery&r is a multiblock that melts many items at once. It can also mix metals together to create alloys. The bigger the Smeltery multiblock, the more it can melt and store.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: Anything that falls into a running Smeltery melts, and that includes you.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Smeltery is a hollow box of seared blocks, which is built in layers:",
    "",
    "- &3Floor&r: One seared block under every empty space inside. The floor doesn't need to reach under the walls.",
    "",
    "- &3Walls&r: A ring of wall blocks around the empty space, on every layer. The corners can be left out.",
    "",
    "- &3Inside&r: Empty, from 1x1 up to 15 blocks wide along the Controller's wall and 8 blocks deep away from it. Put the Controller in the middle of its wall to get the full 15.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "- &aSmeltery Controller&r: In the wall, facing out, with the empty space right behind it.",
    "",
    "- &aSeared Fuel Tank&r: In the wall, filled with lava or another liquid heat. This is where the heat comes from.",
    "",
    "- &aSeared Drain&r: In the wall. A Faucet on the Drain pours the molten metal out of it. Hephaestus blocks don't connect to other mods' pipes.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Walls can be any Seared brick or Seared Stone block, Seared or Clear Glass, Seared Chutes, Ladders and tanks, as well as the Controller and Drain.",
    "",
    "The smallest working Smeltery takes 5 blocks. That's one floor block with the Controller, a Drain, a Fuel Tank and one &2Seared Brick&r around it. A 3x3 Smeltery one layer tall takes 9 floor blocks and 12 wall blocks, and holds 9 items.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Every layer of wall has to be a complete ring. A half-built layer on top stops the whole Smeltery from forming.",
    "",
    "[\"See a finished Smeltery you can turn around in the \", {\"text\": \"Hephaestus GuideMe\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,hephaestus:guide,hephaestus:smeltery.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Smeltery page in the Hephaestus GuideMe\"}, \"underlined\": true}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.7205494CD445A6C0.quest_desc": [
    "Four tools dig, and three of them work over an area.",
    "",
    "Make any mining tool.",
    "",
    "- &aPickaxe&r: Pickaxe Head, Tool Handle, Tool Binding.",
    "- &aSledge Hammer&r: Hammer Head, Tough Handle, two Large Plates. Mines 3x3.",
    "- &aVein Hammer&r: Hammer Head, two Tough Handles, Tough Binding. Mines a whole ore vein.",
    "- &aExcavator&r: Hammer Head, two Tough Handles, Tough Binding. Digs 3x3 of soft ground.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The big tools cost 17 to 19 ingots each, so try the shape in a cheap metal first.",
    "",
    "At level 10 each tool picks one of three mastery paths:",
    "",
    "- &aPickaxe&r: Prospector, Deep Miner or Momentum.",
    "- &aSledge Hammer&r: Demolition, Aftershock or Unstoppable.",
    "- &aVein Hammer&r: Vein Seeker, Chain Reaction or Motherlode.",
    "- &aExcavator&r: Earthmover, Tunnel Shaper or Clean Dig.",
  ],
  "quest.0048109CAC9E47AA.title": "Modifiers",
  "quest.34C064CDD789F0B3.title": "&6The Smeltery",
  "quest.7205494CD445A6C0.title": "Mining Tools",
  "quest.5A9F6DAE3F5A1133.title": "Cast Away",
  "quest.5944FE9E6365D896.title": "Axes",
  "quest.5799EEA11C9946D5.quest_desc": [
    "Molten metal isn't crafted. It's poured.",
    "",
    "Build the three casting blocks so your Smeltery has somewhere to pour.",
    "",
    "- &aSeared Faucet&r: Goes against anything holding molten metal and pours into the block under its spout.",
    "",
    "- &aSeared Casting Table&r: Makes small things like ingots and nuggets.",
    "",
    "- &aSeared Casting Basin&r: Makes full blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.07EC41F08C20D70B.quest_desc": [
    "Every metal so far tops out at Diamond. One goes further.",
    "",
    "Cast an &aEnderium Pickaxe Head&r.",
    "",
    "&2Enderium&r mines at Netherite level, and it is the fastest metal at that tier. It comes from &eFTB Industrial Contraptions&r.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Enderium only melts with &2Molten Blaze&r in the Smeltery's fuel tank. Lava isn't hot enough.",
  ],
  "quest.5A9F6DAE3F5A1133.quest_desc": [
    "The table needs a mold to pour an ingot into, and you make that mold from an ingot you already have.",
    "",
    "Put any ingot on the casting table and pour &2Molten Copper&r over it to get an &aIngot Cast&r.",
    "",
    "The ingot is used up, but the cast lasts forever. Nuggets, gems, plates, gears and rods get their casts the same way, so check JEI when you need one.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Ingot Casts are a great way to make Forge Bricks by pouring Molten Seared Stone from Cobblestone into them.",
  ],
  "quest.0048109CAC9E47AA.quest_desc": [
    "A finished tool can still be improved on the &3Modify&r tab of the Forge Table.",
    "",
    "Put a tool you've made in the Forge Table and look through the Modify tab.",
    "",
    "A tool has five modifier slots. Raising a modifier's level keeps it in the same slot, and each level costs twice as much as the one before.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "- &aReinforced&r: +250 durability per level, up to 5. Starts at 6 Obsidian.",
    "- &aHaste&r: +4 mining speed per level, up to 5. Starts at 4 Blocks of Redstone.",
    "- &aFortune&r: Up to III. Starts at 3 Diamonds.",
    "- &aSilk Touch&r: 6 Echo Shards.",
    "- &aSharpness&r: +1 damage per level, up to 5. Starts at 2 Diamonds.",
    "- &aLooting&r: Up to III. Starts at 4 Emeralds.",
    "- &aSweeping&r: Up to III. Starts at 2 Diamonds.",
    "- &aFlame&r: Sets targets on fire. 8 Blaze Rods.",
    "",
    "Every tool takes Reinforced. Mining tools also take Haste, mining and farming tools take Fortune and Silk Touch, and weapons take Sharpness, Looting, Sweeping and Flame. Silk Touch can't share a tool with Fortune or Looting.",
  ],
  "quest.525277941A4D104D.quest_desc": [
    "Every part has a job, and the material you pick for each one matters.",
    "",
    "- &aHeads&r, Blades and Large Plates: Set durability, mining speed, damage and mining level. When a tool has more than one, their stats are averaged and the first one decides the mining level.",
    "- &aHandles&r: Multiply those stats up or down. A second handle counts for half.",
    "- &aBindings&r: Add flat durability.",
    "",
    "Every material in the tool also brings its trait, so an &2Iron&r Tool Binding gives any tool &3Magnetic&r.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Handles are where most of the difference comes from:",
    "",
    "- &2Enderium&r: +20% durability and +20% mining speed.",
    "- &2Nickel&r: +20% durability and +10% damage.",
    "- &2Aluminum&r: +20% durability.",
    "- &2Invar&r: +15% damage, at the cost of 10% mining speed.",
    "- &2Tin&r: +20% attack speed.",
    "- &2Aurichalcum&r: +15% durability, +10% mining speed and +20% damage, the best of the late handles.",
    "",
    "The Tool Stats panel shows the finished numbers as soon as the parts are in, and nothing is used up until you take the tool, so try a few combinations first.",
  ],
  "quest.34C064CDD789F0B3.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks alloys and bulk melting",
  "quest.4DD55261FDB4BF8A.quest_desc": [
    "Metal parts need a cast, and a cast needs a part to copy.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aPattern&r.",
    "",
    "Put Patterns in a &2Stonecutter&r to cut them into any wooden part. Wooden tools work, but they are the weakest in the game. What they are really for is making your first casts.",
  ],
  "quest.5944FE9E6365D896.quest_desc": [
    "One axe for a single log, one for the whole tree.",
    "",
    "Make an axe.",
    "",
    "- &aHand Axe&r: Small Axe Head, Tool Handle, Tool Binding. Light enough to fight with too.",
    "- &aBroad Axe&r: Broad Axe Head, Tough Handle, Pickaxe Head, Tough Binding. Chops 3x3.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At level 10 each axe picks one of three mastery paths:",
    "",
    "- &aHand Axe&r: Lumber Rhythm, Precision Felling or Hatchet Master.",
    "- &aBroad Axe&r: Timberfall, Falling Giant or War Axe.",
  ],
  "quest.33DCEC2B8CE2D3B2.title": "&6The Forge Table",
  "quest.6223A2A7C3DCF933.title": "Twice the Ore",
  "quest.5DCA31CA513EF27C.title": "Hephaestus",
  "quest.1FA82C79A4A0D17F.title": "Making Casts",
  "quest.33DCEC2B8CE2D3B2.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks tools and weapons",
  "task.4255D0BFBE5CFB8C.title": "Hephaestus Mining Tool",
  "quest.4DD55261FDB4BF8A.title": "Cut From Wood",
  "quest.5C2AFDC4D538BDD3.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSeared Melter&r is an optional smaller version of the Smeltery with a smaller storage.",
    "",
    "Build the &aSeared Melter&r, then place a &2Seared Fuel Tank&r directly underneath it.",
    "",
    "The Melter has no heat of its own. It only burns fuel from a tank right below it, so keep that tank stocked with lava. It holds up to three items and melts them side by side, which is plenty for your first casts.",
  ],
  "quest.05A3BC294BA42FE1.title": "Mastery",
  "quest.7A0968BA22E338AA.quest_desc": [
    "Three blades, from quick to heavy.",
    "",
    "Make a weapon.",
    "",
    "- &aDagger&r: Small Blade, Tool Handle. Fast, light hits.",
    "- &aSword&r: Small Blade, two Tool Handles. Balanced.",
    "- &aCleaver&r: Large Blade, two Tough Handles, Tough Binding. A large two-handed blade.",
    "",
    "A &2Silver&r part adds Smite against undead, and an &aInvar&r handle adds 15% damage.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At level 10 each weapon picks one of three mastery paths:",
    "",
    "- &aDagger&r: Backstab, Flurry or Assassin.",
    "- &aSword&r: Duelist, Executioner or Blade Dance.",
    "- &aCleaver&r: Butcher, Crushing Blow or Bloodlust.",
  ],
  "quest.07EC41F08C20D70B.title": "&dEnderium Edge",
  "task.72434EB0C451D400.title": "Hephaestus Weapon",
  "task.3A0FAE7DDAB52D40.title": "Hephaestus Farming Tool",
  "quest.05A3BC294BA42FE1.quest_desc": [
    "Tools get better the more you use them.",
    "",
    "Use one of your tools until it reaches level 10, then choose its mastery path on the &3Mastery&r tab.",
    "",
    "- &3Mining&r: 5 XP per ore, 3 per log, 2 per other block the tool is made for.",
    "- &3Farming&r: 2 XP per crop.",
    "- &3Fighting&r: XP for every hit based on the damage, plus 5 per kill.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A tool goes up to level 30. The first level takes 100 XP and every level after it takes 20 more.",
    "",
    "At level 10 you choose one of the tool's three mastery paths. The path grows stronger at level 20 and reaches its final form at level 30.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The choice is permanent. A tool can never change its path, so build a second one if you want to try another.",
  ],
  "quest.33DCEC2B8CE2D3B2.quest_desc": [
    "Once you can cast metal, you can cast tools. &eHephaestus Tools&r builds every tool and weapon out of parts, and the &aForge Table&r is where the parts come together.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aForge Table&r.",
    "",
    "- &3Build&r: Pick a tool from the list on the left and put its parts in the slots. The Tool Stats panel shows the finished tool before you take it.",
    "- &3Modify&r: Spend materials to add modifiers to a finished tool.",
    "- &3Mastery&r: Choose a mastery path once a tool reaches level 10.",
  ],
  "quest.7A0968BA22E338AA.title": "Weapons",
  "quest.525277941A4D104D.title": "Heads, Handles and Bindings",
  "quest.5C2AFDC4D538BDD3.title": "Start Small",
  "quest.0C55F4BB9A7A6F2B.quest_desc": [
    "Lava only gets so hot, and some metals need more heat than it can give.",
    "",
    "Melt &2Blaze Rods&r down and fill a bucket with the &aMolten Blaze&r.",
    "",
    "Put it in a &2Seared Fuel Tank&r. Your smeltery can then melt Netherite, Enderium, the Dragonsteels and the Armory metals, which lava can't handle. If a melt makes no progress, check which fuel it needs in JEI.",
  ],
  "quest.0EEBCA59B2927918.quest_desc": [
    "The head's material decides what a tool can mine. Some of the metals at each level:",
    "",
    "- &3Stone&r: Tin, Zinc.",
    "- &3Iron&r: Iron, Copper, Aluminum, Brass, Electrum, Lead, Nickel, Silver.",
    "- &3Diamond&r: Bronze, Invar, Steel, Titanium, Platinum, Uranium, Aquarine Steel.",
    "- &3Netherite&r: Netherite, Enderium, End Steel, Eclipse Alloy and the three Dragonsteels.",
    "- &3Adamantite&r: Adamantite, Aeternium, Aurichalcum.",
    "",
    "&2Bronze&r is the cheapest way to Diamond level, since you alloy it from copper and tin in the Smeltery. A &2Gold&r head mines no better than wood.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Most metals also carry a trait into any tool they're part of:",
    "",
    "- &3Magnetic&r (Iron): Pulls nearby drops toward you.",
    "- &3Dwarven&r (Copper): Mines faster underground.",
    "- &3Lightweight&r (Titanium): Light and quick.",
    "- &3Featherweight&r (Aluminum): Even lighter, acts faster.",
    "- &3Maintained&r (Bronze): Works better while durability is high.",
    "- &3Solid&r (Steel) and &bDense&r (Iridium): Extra durability. Dense is heavier.",
    "- &3Heavy&r (Lead): Slower, but hits harder.",
    "- &3Jagged&r (Ruby): Deals more damage as it wears down.",
    "- &3Shock&r (Electrum): Chance to shock what you hit.",
    "- &3Smite&r (Silver): Bonus damage against undead.",
    "- &3Temperate&r (Desh): Balanced, steady stats.",
    "",
    "Some late metals have traits of their own, like &3Nautical&r on the Nautec metals and an elemental trait on each Dragonsteel. The Tool Stats panel names every trait a part brings.",
  ],
  "quest.045CF1C9896895E7.quest_desc": [
    "These cut crops, and the Mattock digs as well.",
    "",
    "Make a farming tool.",
    "",
    "- &aKama&r: Small Blade, Tool Handle, Tool Binding. Harvests crops.",
    "- &aScythe&r: Large Blade, two Tough Handles, Tough Binding. Harvests 3x3.",
    "- &aMattock&r: Small Axe Head, Tool Handle, Adze Head. An axe and a shovel in one.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "At level 10 each tool picks one of three mastery paths:",
    "",
    "- &aKama&r: Harvest Sweep, Replanter or Green Thumb.",
    "- &aScythe&r: Reaper, Harvest Chain or Death Sweep.",
    "- &aMattock&r: Groundworker, Cultivator or Homesteader.",
  ],
  "task.2D6E56EC38F05D3F.title": "Hephaestus Axe",
  "quest.0C55F4BB9A7A6F2B.title": "Turn Up the Heat",
  "quest.1191F86DE5245E99.quest_desc": [
    "Tools wear out, but you don't have to throw them away.",
    "",
    "Click the gear button at the top of the Forge Table's tool list to open &3Repair and Modify&r, then put in the tool.",
    "",
    "- One of the head's material, such as an ingot for a metal head, restores a quarter of the tool's durability.",
    "- A new part swaps out the old one of that type, and you get the old part back.",
  ],
  "quest.1FA82C79A4A0D17F.quest_desc": [
    "Pour &2Molten Copper&r over any part on a &aSeared Casting Table&r and it hardens into a cast of that part. The part is used up and the cast is kept.",
    "",
    "Make a &aPickaxe Head Cast&r from a wooden Pickaxe Head.",
    "",
    "Fill a cast with any molten metal and you get that part in that metal. The cast is never used up.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each part takes a set amount of metal:",
    "",
    "- &aTool Handle&r and Tool Binding: 1 ingot.",
    "- &aPickaxe Head&r, Small Axe Head, Adze Head and Small Blade: 2 ingots.",
    "- &aTough Handle&r and Tough Binding: 3 ingots.",
    "- &aLarge Plate&r: 4 ingots.",
    "- &aHammer Head&r, Broad Axe Head and Large Blade: 8 ingots.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Parts you no longer need melt back down in the Smeltery.",
  ],
  "quest.5799EEA11C9946D5.title": "Pour Decisions",
  "quest.1191F86DE5245E99.title": "Patch Job",
}